In Part 2 of the Workato CLI series, we move beyond the terminal and start working with a real Workato project locally.

In this video you'll learn how to:

✅ Clone an existing Workato project
✅ Open the project in Visual Studio Code
✅ Explore recipes using the Recipe Visualizer
✅ Make changes locally
✅ Push updates back to Workato
✅ Understand why recipe-lint blocks a push and how to troubleshoot it

This is the workflow every Workato developer should know before integrating GitHub, AI coding assistants, and modern developer practices.

